From: Fanasina <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: platform_profile: Make the class user-selectable

ACPI_PLATFORM_PROFILE is a tristate without a prompt, so it can only be
enabled by a driver that selects it. Give it a prompt so the out-of-tree
diting-platform-profile module can use the class on this arm64 phone.

---
--- a/drivers/acpi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/acpi/Kconfig
@@ -351,7 +351,12 @@ config ACPI_THERMAL
 	  the module will be called thermal.
 
 config ACPI_PLATFORM_PROFILE
-	tristate
+	tristate "Platform profile class (power/performance profiles)"
+	help
+	  Exposes /sys/class/platform-profile/, used by power-profiles-daemon
+	  and desktop environments to switch between power profiles.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
 
 config ACPI_CUSTOM_DSDT_FILE
 	string "Custom DSDT Table file to include"
